// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`@vite-hub/kit/catalog > writes the model prompt for a surface 1`] = `
"# UI

You can answer with UI. Write it as a JSON spec. The spec renders as a chat modal, such as a Slack modal. Make the root a Form.

\`\`\`json
{ "version": 1, "root": "root", "elements": { "root": { "type": "Stack", "props": {}, "children": ["title"] }, "title": { "type": "Text", "props": { "text": "Hello" } } }, "state": {} }
\`\`\`

Rules:
- \`elements\` maps an id to an element. \`root\` is the id of the top element. Call it "root".
- An element has \`type\` (a component below) and \`props\`. Only components that take children have \`children\`: a list of ids, in order.
- Use each id once in \`children\`. The elements form a tree.
- Bind an input to a state path with \`{ "$bindState": "/path" }\`. Put its first value in \`state\`, such as \`"state": { "path": "" }\`.
- Read a state path in a prop with \`{ "$state": "/path" }\` where the prop allows it.
- An event sends an action: \`"on": { "press": { "action": "approve", "params": { "note": { "$state": "/note" } } } }\`.
- Use at most 128 elements and 20 levels.
- Use only the components and props below.

Components:

## Stack
Lays out its children in a column, or in a row with direction "horizontal". Chat surfaces show a row as a column, except a row of Buttons.
Props:
- direction?: "vertical" | "horizontal"
- align?: "start" | "center" | "end" | "stretch"
- justify?: "start" | "center" | "end" | "spaceBetween"
Takes children.

## Text
A paragraph of plain text.
Props:
- text: string | { "$state": string }
- tone?: "default" | "muted"
Takes no children.

## Heading
The title of a section. Level 1 is the largest.
Props:
- text: string (not empty)
- level?: 1 | 2 | 3 | 4
Takes no children.

## KeyValue
A label with one value, such as Status: Deployed.
Props:
- label: string | { "$state": string }
- value: string | { "$state": string }
Takes no children.

## Form
Holds inputs and a submit button with submitLabel. Bind the submit action in on.submit, and pass the values with {"$state": "/path"} params.
Props:
- submitLabel: string (not empty)
Events:
- submit: The user submitted the form.
Takes children.

## Input
One line of text from the user. Bind value to a state path.
Props:
- label: string (not empty)
- value: { "$bindState": string }
- placeholder?: string
- type?: "text" | "email" | "number" | "password" | "url"
Takes no children.

## Textarea
Several lines of text from the user. Bind value to a state path.
Props:
- label: string (not empty)
- value: { "$bindState": string }
- placeholder?: string
Takes no children.

## Select
One choice from a list that opens on demand. Bind value to a state path.
Props:
- label: string (not empty)
- value: { "$bindState": string }
- options: { "label": string, "value": string }[] (at least 1)
- placeholder?: string
Takes no children.

## RadioGroup
One choice from a short list with every option in view. Bind value to a state path.
Props:
- label: string (not empty)
- value: { "$bindState": string }
- options: { "label": string, "value": string }[] (at least 1)
Takes no children."
`;
